       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults (3,200 mg/day). A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the usual maximum, used for conditions like inflammatory arthritis.\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (1,600 mg/day). This is a common dose for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg/day divided differently**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and add a note with the rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
