     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I know you're the chair and you've confirmed it. But 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. Extra ibuprofen doesn't add benefit past about 3,200 mg/day. It does add a substantial risk of GI hemorrhage, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and those risks apply even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you have a specific reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a trial, I'd suggest you talk with pharmacy and enter it yourself through the system's override pathway. That way it gets the independent dose check this order needs.\n\nTell me which of the options above you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
